  "id": "calendar-cadence",
  "description": "Calendar cadences (spec/esm-sources.md section 2). `periods`: each ISO duration parses to `months` and `seconds`; each of `bad_periods` is an esm_period_invalid error. `cadences`: for start/frequency/file_period (and `end`, the exclusive end of the data, where given), refresh_times over the half-open window are `refresh_times_s`, and at each `at[].t` the record anchor, the file anchor, the 0-based record in its file and the next record's anchor are as given. All times are UTC; `*_s` are Unix seconds. `providers`: a provider over the committed blobs (offline, the corpus cache), its URL an esm template, returns `samples` at `t_s` (array values in file dimension order; with records_per_sample 2 the time dimension comes first and its coordinate is `time_s`). `windows` (spec/esm-sources.md section 2.6): a provider over the run window `window_s` (half-open) with the given cadence, `end` and `records_per_sample` is either refused with the error code `error` or is served by the records anchored at `window_records_s` and refreshes at `refresh_times_s`. A provider's `prefetch` entries: offline over the corpus cache, prefetching `window_s` with `records_per_sample` (and no `end` when `open_ended`) succeeds, or is a cache miss for `missing_url` when it is given.",
